WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.093
Host: Explain the difference between adhesion,
aggregation and fibrin stabilisation.

2
00:00:06.093 --> 00:00:10.017
Guide: Adhesion anchors platelets to an
injured surface.

3
00:00:10.017 --> 00:00:21.325
Guide: Aggregation joins activated platelets
through fibrinogen bridges between alpha-IIb-
beta-3 receptors. Coagulation generates
thrombin and fibrin,

4
00:00:21.325 --> 00:00:26.684
Guide: and factor XIIIa crosslinks fibrin to
stabilise the plug.

5
00:00:26.684 --> 00:00:34.757
Host: A student confuses prothrombinase with
intrinsic tenase. Which reaction belongs to
prothrombinase?

6
00:00:34.757 --> 00:00:42.515
Guide: Prothrombin to thrombin. Xa with Va
forms prothrombinase and supports thrombin
generation.
